idity/priority scalars or switch them to a continuous-distribution divergence.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'For validity/impact/priority: per-category COUNT DELTA (stored vs candidate) plus TOTAL VARIATION DISTANCE between the two categorical distributions, computed per stratum and overall.'","decide.py:67-74 validity() returns round(sum(scores)/len(scores), 4) — a continuous [0,1] fraction, not a categorical value.","decide.py:681 priority = round(val * imp, 4) — a continuous derived scalar (validity × impact), with no categorical vocabulary.","verify_models.py defines categorical vocabularies only for the severity ATTRIBUTES (none|low|medium|high, the closed Literal oracle sets) and the binary sub-answers (yes|no|insufficient|na) — there is no per-finding categorical 'validity' or 'priority' axis the verifier emits."],"finding":"The distribution-shift metric is defined over 'validity/impact/priority' as CATEGORICAL distributions (per-category count delta + total-variation distance), but validity and priority are not categorical axes the verifier emits: decide.validity() returns a continuous rounded fraction in [0,1] over the graded binary sub-answers, and priority = validity × impact is likewise a continuous derived scalar. Only impact (the severity attributes / binary answers) has a defined categorical value vocabulary. The plan never defines the category vocabulary (bins) for the validity and priority distributions, so the TVD / per-category count-delta computation over them is unimplementable as written.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f51d71f4285ade7d5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Distribution shift, defined'; and the Compare bullet under 'Approach' ('distribution shift (formula above) for validity/impact/priority')","norm_id":"n834aa6e3493134ef","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor building the tier1 distribution-shift table needs the category set to bin 'validity' and 'priority' counts and compute TVD; with only continuous scalars available, it must invent a bucketing the plan does not authorize, producing metrics that are not comparable across runs.","The κ/agreement table conflates categorical axes (impact severity attrs, binary answers) with continuous ones (validity, priority)."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Restrict the categorical count-delta + TVD to the verifier's genuinely categorical outputs — the severity-attribute enums (none|low|medium|high, the closed Literal oracle sets) and the binary sub-answers (yes|no|insufficient|na) — and for the continuous validity (decide.validity) and priority (validity × impact) scalars, state explicit fixed bins (or use a scalar drift metric), so the metric has a defined value vocabulary.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the finding-count bucket boundaries used as a stratum (e.g. 1 / 2–3 / 4+) so the stratified sample is reproducible and 'respects strata' is testable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan lists strata as 'verdict, leaf/container, finding-count bucket, project overlay/store, impact_model_version' but gives no boundaries for the count bucket","Testing asserts 'sampling is deterministic for a seed and respects strata' — a stratum with undefined edges cannot be checked deterministically","Absence rationale: without fixed boundaries, two implementers (or two edits) produce different strata assignments for the same seed, breaking the reproducibility the approach relies on"],"finding":"The sampling mechanism names a 'finding-count bucket' stratum but never defines its bucket boundaries, leaving the 'deterministic stratified sample [that] respects strata' mechanism under-specified and its reproducibility unverifiable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9a3ab38eef226200","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Sample selection: deterministic stratified sample (strata: ... finding-count bucket ...)'","norm_id":"n30b07d80bb2230c9","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A finding with N findings lands in an ambiguously-bounded bucket, changing stratum membership and thus the sampled set for a fixed seed","The 'respects strata' unit test has no concrete expected bucketing to assert against"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State explicit half-open count buckets (e.g. {1}, {2,3}, {4+}) in the sample-selection description and pin them in the deterministic-sampling unit test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_